    "content": {
      "question_html": "<p>At rest an athlete has a stroke volume of 70 ml and a heart rate of 72 beats per minute. During exercise the stroke volume is 120 ml and the heart rate is 150 beats per minute.</p>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Calculate the cardiac output at rest and during exercise, in litres per minute.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(3)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Explain why stroke volume increases during exercise.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(3)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Cardiac output = stroke volume × heart rate</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Rest: 70 × 72 = 5040 ml = 5.04 litres per minute</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Exercise: 120 × 150 = 18 000 ml = 18.0 litres per minute</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Venous return increases as working muscles squeeze the veins</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">The ventricles fill more and the cardiac muscle is stretched</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">so it contracts with more force (Starling's law) and ejects more blood</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
